  "answer": "This has been reported before: Windows Terminal rewrites the actions/keybindings entries in a different order when it saves settings. The team acknowledged it as a real bug (terminal#13285). The cause is that the entries come from an internal map with no guaranteed sort order for key chords, so the order can change on every save. The ticket records no fix or workaround. Until it is resolved, expect the reordering whenever the Settings UI saves, and consider editing settings.json by hand instead of through the Settings UI to keep diffs clean. You can also follow terminal#13285 for updates."
 },
